DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The bbttssoocckkssttaatt utility symbolically displays the contents of various
     Bluetooth sockets related data structures.  There are few output formats,
     depending on the options for the information presented.  The bbttssoocckkssttaatt
     utility will print results to the standard output and error messages to
     the standard error.

     The options are as follows:

     --hh      Display usage message and exit.

     --MM _c_o_r_e
             Extract values associated with the name list from the specified
             core instead of the default _/_d_e_v_/_k_m_e_m.

     --nn      Show Bluetooth addresses as numbers.  Normally, bbttssoocckkssttaatt at‐
             tempts to resolve Bluetooth addresses, and display them symboli‐
             cally.

     --pp _p_r_o_t_o_c_o_l
             Display a list of active sockets (protocol control blocks) for
             each specified protocol.  Supported protocols are: hhccii__rraaww,
             ll22ccaapp__rraaww, ll22ccaapp,, rrffccoommmm and rrffccoommmm__ss.

     --rr      Display a list of active routing entries (if any) for specified
             protocol.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     The bbttssoocckkssttaatt utility exits 0 on success, and >0 if an error occurs.

